From 32660a2de8a0ae9d8934d1d76c945e013a18ba10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 19:47:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kk: MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=clamp_float_output flushes Inf and
 NaN to 0

DIRT 5 writes Inf and NaN into 1024x1024 sky and transmittance tables. D3D12 flushes them to 0, the format invalid value; Metal keeps them, and the next shader that multiplies one by 0 makes a NaN that turns the race black (a kept Inf lights it white). With clamp_float_output, a float color output that is Inf or NaN becomes 0 in the format-aware fragment pass that already converts the output type.

Class: feature

Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-11-03-dirt5-xbox-minidump-apiset.md

Offered-upstream: no

Generated-by: LLM
